\subtree{
  \title{Closed-Loop Control Experiments}

  \p{
    Closed-loop tokamak control optimizes #{10^5}-weight neural feedback policies solely from trajectory rollouts, without policy gradients, value networks, or replay buffers (Degrave et al. [[Deg+22]](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-021-04301-9), Tracey et al. [[Tra+24]](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fusengdes.2024.114161), Pfau et al. [[Pfa+25]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.00663)). On the \code{toka_gym} TCV rampdown benchmark (Wang et al. [[Wan+25]](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-025-63917-3), Theiler et al. [[The+26]](https://doi.org/10.1088/1741-4326/ae6d12)), we evolve a four-layer policy (#{D = 136{,}712} weights) over #{10{,}000} rounds across #{n = 10} common-random-number seeds (#{800{,}000} total rollouts from initial error \code{58.12 ± 31.39}). Surrogate-free \code{TuRBO-zero} (#{R = 10}) descends identically across all four incumbent-sharing topologies, reaching \code{1.42 ± 0.03} by round #{250} and \code{1.31 ± 0.02} at round #{10{,}000}. Single-region \code{TuRBO-ENN} (#{R = 1}, #{K = 10} neighbors, \code{UCB} acquisition) initially trails \code{R = 10} at round #{250} (\code{1.58 ± 0.05} \code{hyperbolic} to \code{1.68 ± 0.08} \code{euclidean}; exact sign-flip #{p_{\mathrm{Holm}} = 0.014}) while fitting its distance scale, then closes the margin over #{10{,}000} rounds to match \code{R = 10} within paired sampling variation (\code{1.34 ± 0.03} \code{wasserstein}; difference \code{+0.03 ± 0.04}, #{p_{\mathrm{Holm}} = 1.00}).
  }

  \p{
    To test cross-region incumbent sharing under coupled transport physics, we evaluate a #{D = 160{,}531} policy (#{93 \to 256 \to 256 \to 256 \to 19}) over #{10{,}000} rounds in \code{TORAX 2.0.0} (Citrin et al. [[Cit+24]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.06718)), coupling four 1D radial transport equations to Miller local-equilibrium shaping (Miller et al. [[Mil+98]](https://doi.org/10.1063/1.872666)). With the optimizer fixed at surrogate-free \code{TuRBO-zero} (#{R = 10}, #{n = 10} paired seeds), allowing regions to adopt superior incumbents inside their circumscribing Euclidean ball (\code{ellipsoid_ball}) reaches \code{91.57 ± 0.55}, compared with \code{89.41 ± 0.97} for isolated regions (\code{origin_only}). That \code{+2.16 ± 0.91} late separation yields unadjusted paired #{t_9} #{p = 0.0410} at round #{10{,}000}, though it does not survive Holm–Bonferroni correction across six post-initialization checkpoints (#{p_{\mathrm{Holm}} = 0.246}); see [Simulation](simulation.html) for interactive TCV trajectories and \code{FUSE.jl} equilibria (Meneghini et al. [[Men+24]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.05894)).
  }

